                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "As it stands this game has a lot of things working against it.\n\nSmall dev team, slow progress and set backs, empty mmo world with no playerbase, confusing interfase, confusing HUD, poor sound quality, super simplistic and unfun space combat, and no shred of anything ressembling what is in the \"features\" list.\n\nFor instance.\n\n\"Twitch combat\"\nNo, there is no twitch combat.\nThe space combat is slow and plodding, it is literally just lining up your mouse with an enemy and shooting till it dies.\nThe enemies have slow and wide movement paths, and your own ships movement feels extremely unrealistic.\nThere is no sense of feel of thrust, or speed in anything you do.\nYou fly up to an enemy as fast as you can, and stand still as you shoot at it, hoping it doesnt fly out of range making you need to chase it down once again only to stop and keep shooting.\n\n\n\"Why early access?\"\nAccording to the post the dev claims this game needs to be tested with a REAL population.\nWhen I bought this game on march, there is no one on it, and there really hasn't been many people on it since.\nThe dev will NEVER be able to test ANY real numbers on this game going as it is.\n\n\n\"How long till the game releaes?\"\nThe dev claims this game was scheduled to release by christmas last year, but said because of setbacks it would take longer.\nAccording to the post \"I hope these take no more than 6 months\"\nWell assuming that psot was made in december it's still been 8 months since then and there has been no update on the release date.\n\n\n\"What is the current state of the game?\"\nAccording to the dev, all of the \"core features\" are done in this game, but no actual comprehensive list of what features the \"core\" ones are is given.\nAccording to the features list on this page, this game has piracy, mining, bounty hunting, over 800 ships with millions of combinations of gear, and loads of quests to improve your reputation with the many planets and races.\nI can't say for a fact I was in the game long enough to notice if there were really 800 ships and millions of different gear combinations.\nBut what I did see was about 5 available ships to purchase, and something like 20-30 different pieces of equipment.\nEither way the description of what is actualy in the game is vague.\n\n\n\"How are you planning to involve the community in the development of this game?\"\nThe quote given \"“I hope future development will be community driven.”\"\nThis is not an answer.\nLike everything else it's vague or outdated.\nA real answer would be \"I'll be taking suggestions/polls from the community to determine possible future additions to the game\".\n\n\n\nThe developer seems inexperienced, undermanner, and possibly underqualified to see the development of this game through properly.\n\nIf you have a serious interest in indie titles or space sim games, this game is unfinished and has no active player base.\nI myself got a refund for this title and till it turns around I will not be purchasing it.\nThere are a lot of things to be said for not judging a book by it's cover and giving things more of a chance, so it'll be easy to write my review off because of my short time playing the game, but many of the top rated positive reviews of this game have less than an hour or two played in game as well.\nI would suggest waiting till this game releases and see what comes of it.\n\n\nMy suggestion to the development team of this game would be to advertise a free weekend of some sort for this title, inviting a lot of new players into the game.\nThis would properly test the integrity of the servers with lots of players, and might possibly get more players to buy the game after testing it.\nI do hope the games goals come to pass, but right now as it is, I cannot recommend this title.",
